# .dockerignore for the shell-MCP build  --  context = bifrost-router repo root.
#
# The repo root is a 578-file working tree. This image needs TWO files. Deny-all then
# allow by name is therefore the only honest form: a pattern-subtraction .dockerignore
# over this tree is how the router shipped 63 backup files it believed it had excluded
# (see bifrost-router/.dockerignore, the 2026-09-04 K-4 note).
#
# Deny everything.
*
# Allow exactly the two COPY targets. Nothing else is reachable from
# bifrost_shell_static.py (verified: its only non-stdlib import is fastmcp, and its only
# local import is checks; checks.py imports stdlib only).
!checks.py
!bifrost_shell_static.py

# NOT included, deliberately:
#   bifrost_shell.py            -- the FULL tool surface: host paths, LAN endpoints, kubectl.
#                                  Shipping it here would put the host-coupled tools one
#                                  import away from a container that is supposed to be the
#                                  container-safe subset.
#   bifrost_shell_policy.json   -- read by policy_instructions.py in the ROUTER, not by the
#                                  static subset. bifrost_shell_static.py never opens it.
#   requirements*.txt           -- deps are pinned inline in the Dockerfile on purpose
#                                  (fastmcp==3.1.1 tracks the HOST, not the router's 4.0.0b2).
